<pre class='metadata'>
Title: Agent Control Standard
Shortname: acs
Level: 1
Status: LD
URL: https://agentcontrolstandard.ai/spec/
Repository: afogel/ACS_official
Editor: The ACS contributors, OWASP GenAI Security Project https://genai.owasp.org, acs@zenity.io
Abstract: The Agent Control Standard (ACS) is a wire-format specification that lets a
    separate Guardian Agent permit, deny, or modify what an AI agent does in real time,
    over an authenticated channel and with a verifiable audit trail. This document defines
    the ACS-Core baseline — the JSON-RPC envelope, the capability-negotiation handshake,
    the hook taxonomy, the disposition vocabulary, the SessionContext audit chain, replay
    protection, and signature semantics — together with the Trace, Inspect, Provenance,
    Crypto, and Audit conformance profiles that layer observability, component inventory,
    information-flow facts, and cryptographic integrity on top of it.
Markup Shorthands: markdown yes
Local Boilerplate: copyright yes
Default Biblio Status: current
</pre>

